{
  "summary": "This experiment tested weighted fusion in a multimodal model combining RNA (pca_n2000) and image (resnet50) data, achieving validation accuracy of 0.5232 and F1 of 0.5084, slightly lower than the concat fusion baseline (llm_summary_001). The results suggest weighted fusion may not improve performance compared to concatenation, but the role of fusion strategies remains uncertain without direct comparisons to other methods. The multimodal approach still outperforms RNA-only baselines, though fusion method effectiveness requires further isolation."
}

